do CelyneLoop.play_bgm()
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/PART OF YOUR WORLD.png" fade="0.0"]
set {celyna_name} = "???"
set {seyche_name} = "'Goddess'"
join Seyche center [animation="Bounce In" length="0.0"]
join Celyna center
update Seyche left
The Goddess of the sea stood by shore, gazing at the night sky. The moonlight was brighter than what she had seen before. Then, a ripple danced in the water, revealing a figure. Tall, elegant, and balanced between shadow and light.
Celyna: ...
Seyche (Happy): Oh! Hello there, it’s quite rare to see anyone roaming around in these hours.
Celyna: ...
Seyche (Uncomfortable): ... Um...
The Goddess approached her slightly, while still giving a respectful distance from each other.
Celyna: So it is true.
Seyche (Normal): ...
Seyche: What is?
Celyna: You really have returned... Seyche.
The Goddess stood in silence. That name sounded unfamiliar yet it felt like it resonated with her, as though it has always been there. Like it had been waiting. As if, in some forgotten corner of her, it had always fit.
Seyche: That's... a beautiful name.
Celyna: It surely is.
Celyna: Because it's yours.
set {seyche_name} = "Seyche"
Seyche (Surprised): !!
Seyche, the sea Goddess, paused. How could this stranger know her name before she even knew it herself? Could she know more of her past? Or her? More questions kept flooding in unanswered, she didn't know where to begin.
Seyche: ... Then... What's your name?
set {celyna_name} = "Celyna"
Celyna: Forgive me, that was rude of me for not introducing myself, you must be so confused. My name is Celyna. I am the Goddess of the moon.
Seyche (Uncomfortable): No, it’s okay! Was just a bit startled hehe…
Seyche (Normal): ...
Seyche: So, does that mean there are more Gods too? Besides you and I?
Celyna: But of course there are.
The realization that there could be others, Gods sharing the same weight of protecting the islands, somewhat eased her. She wasn’t alone after all.
Seyche: Well, it’s good to know that we’re not entirely holding this up alone!
A warm smile spread across Seyche’s face. The moon goddess paused, her gaze locked onto it. And something in her chest tightened.
A flicker of recognition.
In the silence, the air was filled with unspoken things. Most of them are unknown to Seyche. With a wave rising up to the sand, one decided to break the silence.
Seyche: ...May I ask a question?
Celyna: ...
Celyna: Of course you may, dear.
Seyche: What do you do as a moon goddess, Celyna?
Celyna: Well, it’s quite simple actually.
Celyna: As the goddess of the moon I, too, share in the duty of protecting humanity. In their nights, their dreams, and in their journey under my light.”
Celyna: With each prayer will be answered, whether through direct aid or with gentle guidance.
Celyna: And it seems that you, too, have begun to win the hearts of humanity.
Seyche (Happy): Well, I do want to help them after all.
Celyna: Aren’t you adorable.
As the conversation flowed, the two goddesses began to stroll along the coast side. The waves and the stars kept them company.
Seyche (Normal): Say, Celyna.
Celyna: Yes, my dear?
Seyche: You mentioned there are other gods besides us… who might they be?
Celyna turned to Seyche with an inviting grin, her hand extended to the other goddess.
Celyna: Why don’t you find out instead? Your journey has only just begun.